{
  "case_id": "2001-01-309",
  "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Larry Hope)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JONES: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Under United States v. Lanier, the law was clearly established for purposes of qualified immunity when it gives officials fair warning that their conduct is unlawful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And what should be the rule that you say was violated here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHLICK: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: An official is immune from personal liability for violating Federal rights unless the violation would have been clear to a reasonable officer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But what is the standard that the officers should have been aware of, first in the Eleventh Circuit, and then, assuming that we think we -- that this case presents either the necessity or the proper opportunity for us to say what the national standard ought to be, what is the standard at a more specific level of abstraction than Cruel and Unusual Punishment Clause that we should be dealing with?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Even if -- do you maintain that the issue of whether it was done only to get him to return to the work crew is not in the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Mr. Forster)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the last 15 years, at least eight Federal master judges and eight Federal district judges in Alabama have read the law to hold that handcuffing a prisoner to a restraining bar or to a similar stationary object does not violate the Eighth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the allegations are that he was not given water and not given bathroom breaks."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why doesn't the -- Ort, which you say he's the magistrate on page 89 and 90, supports your position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Missouri, et al.",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We believe this case is controlled by any of three common sense principles of law, each of which is essential if this Court's qualified immunity doctrine is to prevent the problems that it was designed to prevent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "514b2c78bd0ef067295284ce0a485af79a98510ac42bfe25a8d09b7088553592",
      "evidence_id": "ev-514b2c78bd0e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the Court has no questions, we submit that the judgment of the court of appeals should be reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2001-01-309",
